// A carrier `.len` reaches the arithmetic walk with NO carrier of its own, so a
// store that mismatches it escapes the store-conversion check and surfaces as a
// Terminal omission instead. Reduced from `samples/cli/text/text_padding`.
//
//   source                 -> u64 destination   -> i32 destination
//   ordinary `u64` field      checks               IMPLICIT-STORE-CONVERSION
//   carrier `.len`            checks               OMITTED (this fixture)
//
// `let total: u64 = self.message.len;` checks, and so does `.len + 1` into a
// `u64`. The type layer already calls a length `u64`; only the proof layer
// disagrees, and only the mismatch shows it.
//
// The contract is not silent. `wiki/spec/language/counts_and_addresses.md`
// gives Count as "a nonnegative magnitude. General lengths, sizes, and
// compiler-facing policy geometry use `u64`", and says an admitted
// integer-width family "would not change `.len` ... contracts". So a length IS
// a `u64` carrier and this divergence is an implementation gap, not an open
// design question.
//
// Both halves of the gap live in
// `psi/checking/.../arithmetic_domains/expression_analysis/folded_values.rs`:
//
//   - a fixed array with a literal length folds to a POINT interval built with
//     `..NEUTRAL`, which leaves `primitive: None`
//   - a length read off a CONSTRAINED carrier (`[u8; 32] in Utf8`) is refused
//     outright -- deliberately, since a live length differs from capacity --
//     and falls through to the place analysis, which returns NEUTRAL because a
//     `.len` member is not a place
//
// Either way the source primitive is `None`, `check_narrowing_assignment`
// returns before its mismatch arm, and a carrier-less source "keeps landing by
// range": a `[u8; 32]` length fits `i32` on range, nothing rejects it, and the
// Terminal plan has no row to lower it with. Stamping `u64` on the fold, and
// giving the constrained carrier `[0, capacity]` with the same carrier, closes
// both. That file is held by another lane, so the repair is named rather than
// made here.
//
// One caution for whoever makes it: the same `Analysis` feeds arithmetic, so
// stamping a DOMAIN alongside the carrier would put eight green
// `tests/omega/pass/{slices,operators,dependent}` fixtures that do arithmetic
// on a `.len` under overflow proof. The carrier alone is what this store needs;
// leave `domain: None`.
//
// `samples/cli/text/text_padding` asserts in its own header that carrier `.len`
// "resolves uniformly in every value position (guards, host-call args, field
// writes, arithmetic, let bindings)". Measured, one of those five holds:
//
//   guard, uncast (`self.message.len > 5`)          checks
//   field write, uncast                             OMITTED
//   let binding, uncast                             OMITTED (initializer phase)
//   arithmetic, uncast (`16 - self.message.len`)    OMITTED
//   host-call argument, even CAST                   OMITTED (boundary claim
//                                                   transfers -- a different
//                                                   gap, not this one)
//
// Casting at the read (`self.message.len as i32 in Saturating`) or binding it
// to a `u64` local first both check, which is `text_padding`'s own repair.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

domain [u8; 32]::Utf8
requires
    valid_utf8(self);

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    message: [u8; 32] in Utf8;
    width: i32;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.message = "ALERT temp";
    self.width = self.message.len;
    self.console.exit_process(self.width);
}
